  "notes": [
    {
      "kind": "observation",
      "by": "Codex",
      "text": "This export covers only the63-bit stratum. Both frozen protocols share one bounded worker and a native analyzer; rows.csv and analysis outputs contain both strata. Small stratum has30 planned cells; large has6. No profiler attached. Clock values are L0 diagnostics with wall_valid=false; successful recovery and exact certificate checks are counted separately. Every attempted process is retained; no failed cell is excluded. The pod was deleted during63-202-0-x. Its partial clock is null;63-202-0-v andb were not attempted. Original whole-panel analysis correctly refuses incomplete coverage, so its outputs are absent. Separate post-interruption descriptive outputs are not attributed to the frozen script. The canonical format requires attempts>=1, so only four actual large executions appear as runs. Its flow.planned field counts those retained execution records. The frozen protocol still plans six cells; interruption.json retains the two unstarted cells, and the protocol coverage checker must report that infrastructure shortfall."
    }
